# WeddingHub API configuration.
#
# Local run, from the repository root:
#     cp .env.example .env     # then fill in WEDDINGHUB_DATABASE_URL
#     cd backend && go run ./cmd
#
# On a host such as Render, set these as environment variables instead. A real environment
# variable always wins over this file, so nothing here can override a deployment's settings.
# A value containing # must be wrapped in quotes, because # is never treated as a comment.
#
# This file configures the API process only. The browser frontend is pointed at the API with
# `window.WEDDINGHUB_API_URL` or Dashboard -> Settings -> API connection; when the API serves the
# frontend from the same origin it needs no configuration at all.

# Required. PostgreSQL connection string. The API pings it and applies its own migrations at
# startup, and it exits with a fatal error when this is missing or unreachable.
WEDDINGHUB_DATABASE_URL=postgres://weddinghub:secret@localhost:5432/weddinghub?sslmode=disable

# Optional. Listen address. Leave unset and the API uses a PORT injected by the host (Render,
# Heroku, ...), binding every interface, and otherwise falls back to :8080.
# WEDDINGHUB_ADDR=127.0.0.1:8080

# Optional. Directory holding index.html and pages/. Detected automatically when the API is
# started from backend/ (../pages) or from the repository root (pages/); set it when the process
# runs somewhere else, for example /opt/render/project/src.
# WEDDINGHUB_STATIC_DIR=

# Optional. Browser origins allowed to call the API, comma-separated and exact. Loopback origins
# are permitted by default outside production, so this is needed when the frontend and the API
# are served from different hosts.
# WEDDINGHUB_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://your-app.onrender.com

# Optional. Public origin used to build each personal invitation link, for example
# https://your-app.onrender.com. Without it, sending an invitation through the API returns 503
# and the admin dashboard falls back to the browser's own mail or WhatsApp app.
# WEDDINGHUB_PUBLIC_BASE_URL=

# Optional. Where to read this configuration from when it is not .env or ../.env.
# WEDDINGHUB_ENV_FILE=

# Optional. Invitation delivery over SMTP (enables the email channel).
# WEDDINGHUB_SMTP_HOST=
# WEDDINGHUB_SMTP_PORT=587
# WEDDINGHUB_SMTP_USERNAME=
# WEDDINGHUB_SMTP_PASSWORD=
# WEDDINGHUB_EMAIL_FROM=

# Optional. Invitation delivery through the WhatsApp Cloud API (enables the whatsapp channel).
# WEDDINGHUB_WHATSAPP_TOKEN=
# WEDDINGHUB_WHATSAPP_PHONE_NUMBER_ID=
